    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "(2) E-step. Define the weight $ w^{(1)}(k \\mid z_i) $ as the probability that observation $ z_i $ is drawn from distribution $ k $ given the current estimates $ \\widehat{\\sigma}^{2(0)} $, $ \\widehat{\\pi}^{(0)} $, and $ \\widehat{\\mu}^{(0)} $. From Bayes' theorem,",
